2025-05-01 00:59:27 - Thread-156 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns for classifying line‑types  
• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS  
  – "content": holds the complete text of each file; will be split into lines to decide whether a line is ‘trailing’, ‘Space’, or ‘Other’.  
  – "id": unique blob SHA; can be joined to "id" in SAMPLE_FILES if the pathname or repository is needed.  
  – "sample_repo_name": lets us aggregate by repository.  
  – "sample_path": lets us filter by file extension (e.g. *.c, *.py).  
  – "size" / "binary": optional filters (ignore binaries, very small or huge files, etc.).  

• GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES  
  – "id": connects to SAMPLE_CONTENTS."id" (same blob).  
  – "path": alternative file path field.  
  – "repo_name": alternative repository field.  

Typical conditions you may want  
• Exclude binaries → WHERE "binary" = FALSE  
• Only a given extension → WHERE "sample_path" ILIKE '%.c'  
• Ignore very small blobs → WHERE "size" > 0  
• Join files ↔ contents → ON c."id" = f."id"  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (simple → complex) demonstrating how to inspect / aggregate the data.  All identifiers are quoted; each finishes with LIMIT 20.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a handful of files stored in SAMPLE_FILES
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "path",
  "id",
  "mode"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_FILES
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: View the raw text (first 300 chars) of some non‑binary blobs
SELECT 
  "sample_repo_name",
  "sample_path",
  LEFT("content", 300) AS "preview"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "binary" = FALSE
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Distinct repositories present in SAMPLE_CONTENTS
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "sample_repo_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Split one arbitrary file into individual lines
SELECT 
  c."sample_path",
  f.value::STRING AS "line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
  AND c."size" > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Classify lines in a single C source file
SELECT 
  CASE
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$') THEN 'trailing'
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '^[ \\t]+')    THEN 'Space'
    ELSE 'Other'
  END                                          AS "line_type",
  COUNT(*)                                     AS "count"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."sample_path" ILIKE '%.c'
  AND c."binary" = FALSE
  AND c."size" > 0
GROUP BY "line_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Same classification but across ALL non‑binary files
SELECT 
  CASE
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$') THEN 'trailing'
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '^[ \\t]+')    THEN 'Space'
    ELSE 'Other'
  END                            AS "line_type",
  COUNT(*)                       AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY "line_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Top files with largest number of trailing‑space lines
SELECT 
  c."sample_repo_name",
  c."sample_path",
  COUNT(*) AS "trailing_lines"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
  AND REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$')
GROUP BY 
  c."sample_repo_name",
  c."sample_path"
ORDER BY "trailing_lines" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Line‑type counts grouped per repository
SELECT 
  c."sample_repo_name",
  CASE
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$') THEN 'trailing'
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '^[ \\t]+')    THEN 'Space'
    ELSE 'Other'
  END                       AS "line_type",
  COUNT(*)                  AS "cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY 
  c."sample_repo_name",
  "line_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Line‑type percentage per file extension
SELECT 
  SPLIT_PART(LOWER(c."sample_path"), '.', -1)       AS "extension",
  CASE
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$') THEN 'trailing'
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '^[ \\t]+')    THEN 'Space'
    ELSE 'Other'
  END                                               AS "line_type",
  COUNT(*)                                          AS "cnt"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY 
  "extension",
  "line_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: FINAL – overall totals of ‘trailing’, ‘Space’, and ‘Other’ lines
SELECT 
  CASE
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '.*[ \\t]+$') THEN 'trailing'
    WHEN REGEXP_LIKE(f.value::STRING, '^[ \\t]+')    THEN 'Space'
    ELSE 'Other'
  END                         AS "line_type",
  COUNT(*)                    AS "total_occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS c,
     LATERAL FLATTEN( INPUT => SPLIT(c."content", '\n') ) f
WHERE c."binary" = FALSE
GROUP BY "line_type"
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries progress from simple inspection to a full repository‑wide count of each line category without directly returning the requested final numbers.
